---
title: Background
description: background
---
I am a psychologist with a PhD and trained in both the USA and Denmark. Through my work I have met people from many different backgrounds and in many different life situations.

From 2016–2020 I worked as a psychologist in New York, primarily with young people and adults in education. I then moved to Denmark, where I have worked with children and young people—first as a psychologist at PPL in Viborg Municipality and later as a psychologist at Aalborg Municipality.

I am certified in biofeedback, which can be a useful tool for better understanding the links between stress, thoughts, and the body's responses. It can be used, among other things, to work with regulating the body's stress response.

I have also done substantial work with assessment and psychological testing. That has given me a solid understanding of how neuropsychological challenges (for example ADHD and autism) can affect everyday life and contribute to strain, frustration, or a sense of not being able to do everything you want to do.

My professional experience is therefore broad, but what is shared across my work is an interest in people and their resources—and in how we can create better conditions for those resources to come into play, so we can live the life that matters to us. I offer sessions in both Danish and English.
